# broiler-js reference datasets pin 1 (the Intl area)
#
# Broiler.VM's reference datasets of the Intl area, the population of part C of bundle sjl-9-001's rule
# (docs/evidence/sjl-9-001/decision-rule.md, committed at milestone SJL-9.1), which takes "Broiler.VM's
# reference datasets of the area, byte for byte as Broiler.VM's commit that carries its own bundle sjl-9-001
# rule holds them, each with Broiler.VM's retained answer and divergences file: src/tests/cldr/{dates,
# displaynames, durations, lists, locales, numbers, plurals, relativetimes, segments}/ and
# src/tests/temporal/{intl, calendars-intl, zone-names}/, which SJL-9.2 copies into conformance/datasets/intl/
# with their digests and the pin conformance/datasets/intl/datasets.pin; and src/tests/cldr/timezones/, which
# conformance/datasets/time/ holds since SJL-8.4 under block 1 of its datasets.pin; a copy whose digest differs
# is not the population". This file pins the first twelve programs, copied on 2026-10-26 (milestone SJL-9.2,
# work package SJL-9.2a). The thirteenth, timezones.js, stays where block 1 of
# conformance/datasets/time/datasets.pin pins it, and the harness reads it from there.
#
# WHERE THEY CAME FROM. The commit that carries Broiler.VM's bundle sjl-9-001 rule is
# 4cf9ca449fc96a1a5be810f6d0ca31c42b855c8f, the merge of Broiler-Platform/Broiler.VM#171, which holds
# docs/evidence/sjl-9-001/decision-rule-area.md and JSD-0082. Each file below was written by
# `git cat-file blob <source-commit>:<path>` in a Broiler.VM checkout, from the commit's object and not from a
# working tree. Its Git blob id is the one Broiler.VM's tree at that commit names for the path, so
# `git -C <Broiler.VM> rev-parse <source-commit>:<path>` prints it. The same blobs are those of Broiler.VM's
# 01444a5, whose objects docs/evidence/sjl-9-001/divergence-groups.tsv names each divergences file by, and of its
# cd1928d, the revision the correspondence ran: `git diff --stat 01444a5 4cf9ca4 -- src/tests/cldr
# src/tests/temporal` and `git diff --stat cd1928d 4cf9ca4 -- src/tests/cldr src/tests/temporal` print nothing.
# Each divergences file is `divergences.txt` in Broiler.VM, so it is renamed here after its program, as SJL-8.4
# named the time area's; nothing else is renamed, and no byte is changed. `orderings` (SJL-17's) is not copied.
#
# WHAT A LINE MEANS. As in conformance/datasets/time/datasets.pin: `source-commit <commit>` names the Broiler.VM
# commit of the `file` lines after it, up to the next `source-commit` line; `copied` says when that block was
# copied. `file <name in this directory> <bytes> <sha256> <git blob id> <Broiler.VM path at the block's
# source-commit>`. `program <name> <program> <retained answer> <divergences>` says which three files make one
# program's dataset. The harness, scripts/conformance/run_reference_datasets.py, refuses to run when a file's
# length or SHA-256 differs from its line, and its tests hold every file to its line, and its blob id to its
# bytes, on every run of the conformance scripts' tests. To check by hand, in this directory:
#
#   awk '$1 == "file" { print $4 "  " $2 }' datasets.pin | sha256sum -c

source-repository Broiler.VM
source-commit 4cf9ca449fc96a1a5be810f6d0ca31c42b855c8f
copied 2026-10-26
licence-programs Apache-2.0
licence-answers none (outputs; see README.md and THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md)
